    "chunk_text": "(2) The first Board of directors of the Corporation shallconsist of the members of the Board of Directors of the Instituteholding office of the day immediately preceding the date ofcommencement of this Act.\n\n6.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from time totime at any general meeting and by a majority of not lessthan two-third of the members present and voting, to makerules, not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act, or anyother written law, for all or any of the following matters:\u2014\n\n(a)Classification of membership, admission,withdrawal or expulsion of member;\n\n(b)The election of the members of the Board ofDirectors, the resignation from, or vacation of orremoval from office and their powers, conduct andduties;\n\n(c)The powers, conduct duties and functions of thevarious officers, agent and servants of theCorporation;\n\n(d)The procedure to be observed for the summoningand holding of meetings of the Board of Directors,the times, places, notices and agenda of suchmeeting, and the conduct of business;\n\nRules of theCorporation.\n\nLasallian Community Education Services(Incorporation)5\n\n(e)The administration and management of theproperty of the Corporation; and\n\n(f)Generally, for the management of the affairs of theCorporation and the accomplishment of its objects.\n\n(2) Any rule made by the Corporation may be amended,altered, added to or repealed in like manner at a like meetingas a rule made under subsection (1).\n\n(3) The members of the Corporation shall be subject tothe rules of the Corporation.\n\n7.(1) The Corporation shall have its own Fund. and allmonies heretofore or hereafter to be received by way of gifts,bequests, donations, subscriptions, contributions, fees orgrants on behalf of the Corporation shall be deposited to thecredit of the fund of the Corporation in one or more Banksas the Board of Directors may determine."
