    "chunk_text": "(2)in subsection (1A) by the repeal of paragraph (c)thereof and the substitution therefor of the followingparagraphs:\u2014\n\n\u201c(c)has passed the special examinationprescribed in that behalf by the MedicalCouncil; and\n\n(d)holds a certificate granted by the MedicalCouncil under subsection (3) of section43A,\u201d;\n\n\u201c(2) The fee for registration as a dentist shall bea prescribed amount payable on application to theregistrar.\u201d.\n\nAmendmentof section 43of Chapter105.\n\nMedical (Amendment)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(4)by the insertion immediately after subsection (3)thereof of the following:\u2014\n\n\u201c(4) Any dentist who obtains a qualificationwhich is prescribed as a specialist qualificationrecognized by the Medical Council shall be issuedwith a specialist dentists licence for a prescribedperiod on payment of the prescribed fee, subject tosuch terms and conditions stipulated in suchlicence.\u201d.\n\n3.The following sections are hereby insertedimmediately after section 43 of the principal enactment andshall have effect as sections 43A and 43B thereof:\u2014\n\n43A. (1) A person shall make and applicationto the Medical Council for provisionalregistration as a dentist solely for the purposeof acquiring experience required by theMedical Council for obtaining a certificateunder subsection (3), if he\u2014\n\n(a)is of good character;\n\n(b)is a citizen of Sri Lanka; and\n\n(c)(i)holds a Degree of Bachelor ofDental Surgery of the Universityof Ceylon or a correspondingUniversity or a Degree AwardingInstitute; or\n\n(ii)has passed the examinationnecessary for obtaining the Degreeof Bachelor of Dental Surgery ofthe University of Ceylon or acorresponding University or aDegree Awarding Institute, but has\n\n\u201cProvisionalregistrationof dentists.\n\nInsertion ofnew section43A and 43Bin theprincipalenactment.\n\n3Medical (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30"
