    "chunk_text": "(3) All applications for Membership shall be on aSLACD application form approved by the Council andpresented to the Secretary of the SLACD or his/herdelegate. As indicated under Section 4 (3), the applicationshould include a recommendation by relevant authority. TheSecretary shall review each application for suitability tobe admitted to SLACD and submit with recommendationsto the Council. The Council shall take the final action.\n\n(5) The Annual Meeting of members shall be held at suchtime and place as shall be determined by the council of theSLACD. Such meetings shall be held for the transaction ofsuch business as may properly come before the meeting.The Annual Meeting shall consist of scientific sessionswhenever possible. Recognition of new members shall takeplace at each Annual Meeting.\n\n(6) Special meetings may be called by the President ofthe SLACD by a majority of the council or upon petition of15 or more of the Members of the SLACD.\n\n(7) Written or printed notice of each meeting of Membersof the SLACD, stating the place, day, and hour of the meetingand, in case of a special meeting, the purpose or purposes for\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n35\n\nSri Lanka Association for Child Development(SLACD) (Incorporation)6\n\nwhich the meeting is called, shall be delivered not less thanfive (5) or more than sixty (60) days before the date of themeeting, either personally or by mail, to each Member. Ifmailed, such notice shall be deemed to be delivered whendeposited in the Sri Lanka Post, addressed to the Member athis most recent address as it appears on the register of theSLACD."
