    "chunk_text": "5.(1) Upon the recommendation of the Council, anyMember of any class may be expelled by an affirmative voteof three-fourths of the Membership present at an AnnualMeeting of the SLACD, provided that a copy of the chargesagainst him/her with a written notice of the hearing thereonby the Council at a special time and place, shall have beendelivered to him/her personally or mailed to his/her lastknown address, not less than 90 days before the date of suchhearing, and further provided, that the Member charged shallhave the right to appear before the Council in defense of thecharges.\n\n(3) Any Member of the SLACD in good standing mayrequest of the Council a leave of absence for a period of notmore than two years. When a Member so requests, a waiver ofdues during the leave of absence may be granted by theCouncil. Any further extension of the leave of absence shallbe dependent on the Member submitting a request for furtherextension, and favourable action on the request by theCouncil.\n\n6.(1) Except as otherwise provided by these by-laws,the powers of the SLACD shall be exercided, its propertycontrolled, and its affairs conducted by the Council of SLACD.\n\n(2) The Council shall consist of fifteen (15) members:Seven (7) elected officers. The President, Vice-President,President-elect, two Secretaries, Treasurer, AssistantTreasurer, Two (2) most recently retired Presidents of theSLACD, Four (4) members from the General Membership, three(3) of whom shall represent Paediatrics, Child and AdolescentPsychiatry and Allied Health professionals, one each.\n\nCancellationofMembership.\n\nPower of theCorporation.25\n\n30\n\nSri Lanka Association for Child Development(SLACD) (Incorporation)8\n\nTwo non-voting members shall represent the Sri LankaCollege of Paediatricians, College of Community Physicians."
