    "chunk_text": "6.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall, subject to therules in force for the time being fo the Corporation, beadministered by a Board of Administration consisting ofsuch number of persons as may be provided for in such rulesand appointed periodically by the Life Patrons at their solediscretion.\n\n(3) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from time to time,at the discretion of the Life Patrons to make rules, notinconsistent with the provisions of this Act or any otherwritten law.\n\n(4) Any such rule made may be amended, altered or addedto, or rescinded at the discretion of the Life Patrons.\n\n(5) The lands and buildings of the Institute is the propertyof the Late Founder His Holiness Assaiyyidh AsshheikhKoya Thangal Al-Qadhiriyyah War-Rifa\u2019iyyah(Qaddasallahu Sirrahul Azeez) and his heirs and successors.\n\n7.(1) The Corporation shall have its own fund andmoneys received by the Fund of the way of testamentarydispositions, transfers, donations shall be deposited in thename of the Corporation in one or more banks as the LifePatrons shall determine.\n\n(2) All expenses borne by the Corporation in the exerciseand discharge of powers and functions of the Corporationshall be paid out from the fund.\n\n8.The Corporation shall be able and capable in law, toacquire and hold any property movable or immovable whichmay become vested in it by virtue of purchases, holdproperty grants, gifts, testamentary disposition immovable or\n\nFund of theCorporation.\n\nRules of theCorporation.\n\nCorporationmay holdpropertymovable andimmovable.\n\n5Al-Jamiathul Ghawsiyyah (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\notherwise and such property movable and shall be held bythe Corporation for the purposes of this Act and subject tothe rules in immovable force for the time being of theCorporation and it shall have the full power to sell, mortgage,lease, exchange or otherwise dispose of the same at thediscretion of the Board of Administration."
