    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of November 06, 2015\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 09. 11. 2015)\n\nPENAL CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Justice\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause inserts new section 291c in the Penal Code (Chapter 19) and thelegal effect of the section is to make provision to convict and punish persons who cause orinstigate acts of violence or hostility which lead to religious, racial or communal disharmonybetween different racial or religious groups.\n\n1Penal Code (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n2\u2014PL 009335\u2014425 (10/2015)\n\nShort title.\n\nL. D.\u2014O. 28/2015.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PENAL CODE (CHAPTER 19)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Penal Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2015.\n\n2.The following section is hereby inserted immediatelyafter section 291B of the Penal Code (Chapter 19) and shallhave effect as section 291C of that Code:\u2014\n\n291C. Whoever, by the use of words spoken,written or intended to be read, or by signs, orby visible representation, or otherwise, intendsto cause or attempts to cause or instigates orattempts to instigate, acts of violence orreligious, racial or communal disharmony, orfeelings of ill-will or hostility, betweencommunities or different classes of persons ordifferent racial or religious groups, shall bepunished with imprisonment of eitherdescription for a term which may extend totwo years.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nInsertion ofnew section291C inChapter 19.\n\n\u201cCausing ofor instigatingacts ofviolence,hostility, etc.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\nPenal Code (Amendment)2"
