    "chunk_text": "2.From and after the date of commencement of thisAct, such and so many persons as now are members of the\"Child Rehabilitation Centre\" (hereinafter referred to as\"the Centre\") or shall herafter be admitted as members of theCorporation hereby constituted shall be a body corporatewith perpectual succession, under the name and style of the\"Child Rehabilitation Centre\" (hereinafter referred to as the\"Corporation\") and by that name may sue and be sued andshall have full power and authority to have and use a commonseal and to alter the same at its pleasure.\n\n(a)to stop all forms of violence against children;\n\n(b)to distribute all types of humanitarian assistance tothose subject to violence, refugees and children,adults and the disabled and poor communities inneed of such assistance;\n\nIncorporationof the ChildRehabilitationCentre.\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n30\n\nChild Rehabilitation Centre (Incorporation)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(c)to assist socio-economic development of ruralcommunities by maintaining activities in the fieldsof fisheries, small enterprises and rural industriesthrough participatory development ;\n\n(d)to uplift living standards of rural poor people byincome generating activities, self employmentopportunities and by making all kinds of attemptsneeded for implementing skills developmentprograms;\n\n(e)to be committed to protect health, educational,gender rights of those affected by war and sociallybackward groups and the rights of children and tocontribute to social development by implementingprograms required for their capacity development;\n\n(f)to develop leadership skills of women whileempowering them; to form and maintain women'sgroups and implement projects to make womencontribute to socio-economic development;\n\n(g)to implement academic and training programsrelevant for environment conservation of rural areas;\n\n(h)to take all possible steps for the peace,understanding and co-existence of the oppressedgroups; and"
